        <activityName xml:lang="en">Allyl chloride, from reacting propylene and chlorine, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Allyl chloride, from reacting propylene and chlorine, at plant
Liquid propene is  reacted  with gaseous chlorine;
UUID: 6c5773d2-f0a9-3117-95fa-6f371a29996f
Multi-output process that produces three outputs from the reaction of propylene with chlorine: allyl chloride, hydrochloric acid (36wt%) and 1,3-dichloropropene.
Location: RER
Technology: based on industry data in the US and Europe
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: &lt;null&gt;
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_6c5773d2-f0a9-3117-95fa-6f371a29996f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
